### 5.3 Sequential double-run determinism

House Law §5.3 requires every probe to run twice in fresh processes with `Run_1 == Run_2`. The test binary output and the
`--json` output were compared byte-for-byte:

| Repository | test-binary output | `--json` output |
|---|---|---|
| oosysbus | BYTE-IDENTICAL (123 assertion lines) | BYTE-IDENTICAL |
| oovfs | BYTE-IDENTICAL (148 assertion lines) | BYTE-IDENTICAL |
| ooflash | BYTE-IDENTICAL | BYTE-IDENTICAL |
| oobrowser | BYTE-IDENTICAL | BYTE-IDENTICAL |
| oocanvas | BYTE-IDENTICAL | BYTE-IDENTICAL |
| oochat | BYTE-IDENTICAL | BYTE-IDENTICAL |
| oodaw | BYTE-IDENTICAL | BYTE-IDENTICAL |
| oodeck | BYTE-IDENTICAL | BYTE-IDENTICAL |

Note on method: a whole-`make test` byte-comparison reports a false "DIFFERS" because run 1 rebuilds the binary and run 2 reuses
the cached artefact, so only the build chatter differs. The comparison above excludes the build line and compares the assertion
output itself; the Makefile's own `cmp -s .ooda-cache/r1.txt .ooda-cache/r2.txt` gate (`PASS: double-run output determinism`)
also passed in every repo.

