## 7. Residual findings

**F1 — dead `std/hw/*` import prefix.** Three repos were temporarily uncompilable at HEAD on this path; fixed upstream (§3.1).
Any repo outside the eight that still imports `std/hw/...` will fail import resolution. A fleet-wide grep for `import "oostd/hw/`
is recommended.

**F2 — the toy modulus was never a *correct* modulus.** `1000000007` was used in two different roles across the fleet: as a
packing modulus in the item codec, and as a hash salt in `oo_pqc_sha3_round` calls. The second role is the more dangerous one: a
salt is a *distinct input* to a hash, so a value that reads like "the modulus" silently became the fleet's hash salt. The
remediation standardises that salt to `7` fleet-wide, matching what upstream had already done in oochat/oobrowser/oocanvas. A
repository-wide audit for `oo_pqc_sha3_round(..., <non-7 salt>)` would confirm no other repo drifted.

**F3 — the Black Hat traversal heuristic has a narrow exemption.** The marker `_expect_` must appear with underscores on
**both** sides. A helper named `ooflash_fx_expect` does **not** satisfy it; `ooflash_expect_fx` does. This bit the first attempt
at the ooflash fix and is worth knowing before the next page in the fleet needs the same treatment.

---

## 8. Artifacts

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `audits/tools/scan/oohat_scan.oo` | Faithful re-implementation of the Purple + Black gates; reproduces the real oohat exactly |
| `audits/tools/scan/import_audit.oo` | Import-resolution audit against the compiler's sibling-prefix rules |
| `audits/tools/scan/remediate_toy.oo` | The remediation, with asserted before/after occurrence counts (fails loudly on drift) |
| `audits/tools/sweep/oohat_sweep.oo` | lint + `make verify` + `make test` ×2 sweep |
| `audits/tools/sweep/determinism.oo` | Strict assertion-level double-run determinism check |
| `audits/tools/sweep/oohat_commit.oo` | Per-repo commit script with the tailored messages |
| `audits/logs/` | Per-repo lint / verify / test / determinism logs |

## 9. Environment notes

- `oodac` wrapper enforces `timeout --kill-after=5s 240s` with a 2-slot concurrency limit and a per-repo `flock` at
  `/tmp/oodac-slots`; under fleet load builds fail with `Error 124`. Verification was run against
  `/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac.real` with `OODA_COMPILER`/`OODAC_BIN` exported.
- `oodac.real build` requires `OODA_COMPILER` or `OODAC_BIN` in the environment, else
  `ERR build OODA_COMPILER or OODAC_BIN required`.
- `lint-oo-size` requires `OODA_NO_JAIL=1`, else it errors with "no lint root is readable under /Projects/openOODA".
- `/Projects/openOODA-core/` was not modified: `std`, `std-hw`, and `oodac` belong to another agent's claim (`w3:p1`).
